Package: homelab-haproxy
Architecture: all
Depends: perl (>= 5.36), libyaml-libyaml-perl, libmojolicious-perl, homelab-common (>= 0.1.19), haproxy
Description: HAProxy TCP-passthrough edge for the homelab-* ecosystem
 Ships homelab-haproxy-apply-backends, which reads an editable
 /etc/homelab/haproxy/backends.yml (frontend port -> backend host:port
 pairs) and regenerates /etc/haproxy/haproxy.cfg wholesale, validating
 with `haproxy -c` before ever touching the live config. Exists to
 decouple "holds the public IP" from "runs the actual service" for raw
 TCP protocols (SMTP, IMAP, ...) that, unlike HTTP, homelab-webproxy's
 nginx-based reverse proxy can't front on its own -- lets services like
 homelab-postfix/homelab-dovecot move off the internet-facing host
 while their ports keep working from the same public IP. Does not (and,
 being HAProxy, structurally cannot) proxy UDP -- DNS's primary query
 traffic is out of scope for this tool.
